            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0731" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.30/51: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-22T23:00:00+01:00">October 22,
                            1943—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 22—12:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3083. My 293 [<hi rendition="#italic">2933</hi>] October 10. I discussed Italian
                    warships in Balearics again with Jordana today. I said legal status clear and
                    Spain should release ships promptly. There were more than 2,000 seamen involved
                    and I was sure the Spanish authorities would not want any trouble at Port Mahon.
                    He said both he and Minister of Marine greatly impressed by arguments set forth
                    in my note 1444 of October 12 (see my despatch 1441, October 12) and he hoped to
                    reply very speedily. I said I trusted the decision would be favorable and he
                    replied that our arguments were very strong.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
